      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors report 10 cases of pain in the outer surface of the hip related to damage of the perforating lateral branch of the subcostal or ilio-hypogastric nerve, which innervate this region. Anatomic investigation showed that there was a possibility of canal neuropathy, the possible mechanisms and signs of which are discussed. In general, treatment consisted of local infiltrations, but one patient underwent surgery with highly successful results."},
